<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_GenStep_LiquidShores.xml                  WORLDMAP_LIQUID_TAGS_1, half 2
  ============================================================================
  The landing repaint: a map generated on a tile belonging to a TYPED body
  (RM_LiquidBodyRegistry.xml) has its standing water repainted to that
  liquid's terrain suite. On an untyped tile the step reads the tag, gets
  null and returns having touched nothing.

  ORDER 245, and the number is not arbitrary. Core's own steps:
      210  Terrain                  <- generates the water this repaints
      220  MutatorPostTerrain       <- mutators get their terrain edits in
      240  RemoveTinyIslands
    * 245  RM_GenStep_LiquidShores  <- here
      390  Roads
  So it runs after everything that AUTHORS terrain and before anything that
  places structures on top of it, which means a road, a ruin or a set-piece
  is never repainted out from under itself.

  It draws no random numbers, so its position costs nothing in world
  determinism; SeedPart is distinct from every vanilla step's purely so the
  seed-part de-duplication in MapGenerator.GetSeedPart does not fold it in
  with a neighbour.

  Registration is via Patches/RM_LiquidShores_MapGenPatch.xml, onto the
  shared MapCommonBase generator — the same self-gating shape
  RUT_FungalSoilScatter already uses. That is safe precisely because the step
  no-ops on every untyped tile.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>RM_LiquidShores</defName>
    <order>245</order>
    <genStep Class="RimMandrake.FlowWorks.LiquidTypes.RM_GenStep_LiquidShores" />
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
